map( ) FUNCTION
----------------
- The map( ) function is used for applying some logic on each and every element available in
  a sequence
- map( , ) will take two parameters
- First Parameter is Lambda Function and second parameter is sequence
Syntax:- map(lambdafunction, list)

Eg.
sal = [7000, 5000, 12000, 8000, 6000]
if you want to add 3000 in every sal 

sal = [7000, 5000, 12000, 8000, 6000]
newsal=[]
for i in sal:
    newsal.append(i+3000)
    
print(*newsal)
output
------
10000 8000 15000 11000 9000

LAMBDA
------
sal=[7000,1000,6000,5000]
newSal=list(map(lambda s:s +3000,sal))
print(*newSal)

output
------
10000 4000 9000 8000


filter( , ) FUNCTION
--------------------
-- It is used to filter Given List according to your requirement
-- filter( , ) function is used to bring specific elements from a sequence
-- filter( , ) will take 2 inputs
Syntax: filter( lambda , list )

Eg.
---
sal=[7000,1000,6000,5000]
filterData=list(filter(lambda s:s>5000,sal))
print(*filterData)

Output
------
7000 6000

reduce( ) FUNCTION
------------------
- This function can be applied on two arguments and finally it gives aggregate value in a
  sequence
- reduce( ) function is available in a module, i.e : functools
- reduce( ) function by default takes group of values as a input, then it gives single value as a
  result. but at the time of taking input it takes two values at once.
Example
-------
Aggregation visual logic for list a = [5, 7, 2, 4, 3]:
5 + 7 -> 12
12 + 2 -> 14
14 + 4 -> 18
18 + 3 -> 21 (Final aggregate value)

import functools
l1=[10,20,30,10]
res=functools.reduce(lambda p,q:p+q,l1)
print(res)

output
------
70


Ex: Parking Lot Monitor
A sensor in each parking bay sends a signal to your system:
1 means a car is currently parked there (Occupied).
0 means the spot is empty (Available).
The sensors send these signals as an array. Your job is to tell the driver exactly 
which index (spot number) they should drive to. Drivers want the first available spot to save time.

Input Array: [1, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0]
Output: 3 (The app tells the driver: "Go to Spot #3")
Input Array: [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0]
Output: 6
Input Array: [1, 1, 1, 1]
Output: "Parking Full"


def find_parking_spot(data): 
    for i in range(len(data)): 
        if data[i] == 0: 
            return i + 1 
    return "Parking Full" 
 
print(find_parking_spot([1, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0])) # 3 
print(find_parking_spot([1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0])) # 6 
print(find_parking_spot([1, 1, 1, 1]))       # Parking Full 	 


